      "language": "zh+en",
      "prompt": "B. From only this fictional contract draft an English abstract115–140words and one candidate contribution≤40words. Approved English proposed name ScaleQueryFD, no approved Chinese full name, novelty comparison pending. Task: known-class fault classification from a multivariable industrial-process window. Parallel convolutional branches encode the same window at two temporal resolutions, U and V. Queries come from coarse U; keys/values come from concatenated[U;V]. Two heads use separate projections; concatenate their feature outputs and apply a learned output projection. The transformed attention output is added to a dimension-matched U bypass, then mean-pooled across U's sequence positions and classified. All measurements lie within a completed window available before issuing its endpoint decision; prediction weights are fixed. There are no separately acquired modalities, predefined production-stage groups, physical graph, variable mask, interpolation or train/test parameter updates. A single simulated process benchmark case has lower classification error than the same encoder/predictor without the cross-scale attention path. No physical-causal, cross-plant, source-independent, real-world deployment, probability-calibration, early-warning or runtime claim is tested. Link multiscale encoding -> actual query/context interaction -> residual summary -> endpoint class decision -> the actual ONE benchmark comparison. Do not turn temporal scales into production stages, invent two case studies or claim ordinary attention alone is novel. Keep author-only verification/novelty notes separate from positive prose, without a defensive closing checklist. State exact word counts.",
